id: core/node
title: "core node"
kind: mental-model-node
status: v1
updated: 2026-07-21

purpose: >
  Hold the public core concepts for understanding and using .yawn.

holds:
  - what a yawn is
  - orientation
  - memory update
  - movement frame
  - movement loop
  - lacuna
  - agency
  - observer and body
  - proof and boundary
  - folder-node protocol
  - state substrate and event reduction
  - optional target conditions and typed lacunae
  - state transition intent and result
  - motivation and purpose

receives:
  - readme.yawn
  - shape primitives
  - scientific frame
  - bridge-layer core files

produces:
  - public ontology terms
  - safe movement rules
  - reusable mental models

questions:
  - what is the smallest true concept here
  - how does movement stay bounded
  - what does proof protect

links:
